+  <p class="muted">Phase 6 local pilot: the bursar's registered workbook is the live destination.</p>
+  <section><h2>Starting the application</h2><p>Double-click <strong>START CASHBOOK.bat</strong> and keep that window open. The browser interface will open automatically.</p></section>
+  <section><h2>1. Register the live cashbook</h2><p>Choose the actual `.xls` workbook the bursar normally captures into. The application parses its monthly PC/RC sheets and category columns, stores that workbook as the managed live cashbook, and writes approved transactions into that same file.</p><p><strong>No second cashbook is generated.</strong></p></section>
+  <section><h2>2. Import a Standard Bank statement</h2><p>Upload CSV, XLS or XLSX. The application validates transaction structure, detects duplicates, and reconciles the running balances before accepting the statement.</p></section>
+  <section><h2>3. Review exceptions</h2><p>Trusted exact historical classifications are approved automatically. New, fuzzy or uncertain classifications appear in the review table. Saving a classification immediately attempts to sync that transaction into the live cashbook.</p></section>
+  <section><h2>4. Check the cashbook</h2><p>Use <strong>Live cashbook preview</strong> to see the target sheet, category and sync state. Click <strong>Open cashbook in Excel</strong> when you want to inspect the actual workbook.</p><p>If Excel already has the workbook open while the app needs to write, close Excel and click <strong>Sync cashbook now</strong>.</p></section>
+  <section><h2>Safety</h2><p>Imported bank transactions are fingerprinted. Synchronized cashbook rows are tracked separately, so retrying sync cannot append the same transaction again. If an already-synced category is corrected, the original row is reallocated rather than duplicated. A cashbook backup is created before each write.</p></section>
+  <section><h2>If something goes wrong</h2><p>Look for an error ID such as <code>ERR-20260831-12AB34CD</code>. Download the support bundle and send both to the developer.</p></section>
 </body>
 </html>
